index 9407145..a11b7e9 100644
--- a/kernel/rng.c
+++ b/kernel/rng.c
@@ -1,123 +1,358 @@
-/* kernel/rng.c — seeded xorshift128+ pool (POSIX2024 phase Q16).
+/* kernel/rng.c — kernel CSPRNG (INTERNET_PLAN.md phase N0).
  *
- * The boot-time syscalls used a per-call rdtsc-xorshift filler with no
- * persistent state.  This module keeps a 128-bit xorshift128+ state that is
- * seeded from every entropy-ish source the kernel already has:
+ * Replaces the Q16 seeded xorshift128+ pool.  The generation core is the
+ * ChaCha20 DRBG in kernel/rng_core.h; this file is responsible for the
+ * ENTROPY feeding it, which is the part N0 exists for (decision D1: no
+ * cryptographic code may stand on a guessable seed).
  *
- *   - RDRAND, when CPUID.1:ECX.RDRAND is set (QEMU exposes it with
- *     -cpu qemu64? no — qemu64 lacks RDRAND, so this is a genuine
- *     "when available" path, exercised on real hardware and newer vCPUs);
- *   - RDTSC and the PIT tick counter;
- *   - the addresses of kernel objects (ASLR-ish layout noise);
- *   - the current stack pointer.
+ * Sources, in preference order:
  *
- * The mixing function is SplitMix64, which turns the loosely-correlated
- * seed words into a well-distributed 128-bit state.  xorshift128+ is a
- * fast, well-understood PRNG (Vigna 2017); it is NOT a cryptographic
- * generator.  That is stated in TODO.md, not overclaimed: getrandom(2)
- * must not be advertised as /dev/urandom-equivalent.
+ *   1. RDSEED  — CPUID leaf 7 EBX bit 18.  A wide hardware entropy source;
+ *                384 bits (48 bytes) are collected with a bounded retry,
+ *                since RDSEED is allowed to return CF=0 when its pool is
+ *                drained.
+ *   2. RDRAND  — CPUID leaf 1 ECX bit 30.  Conditioned hardware source;
+ *                used when RDSEED is absent or starved.
+ *   3. Interrupt-timing jitter pool — the fallback.  irq_dispatch() calls
+ *                rng_jitter_event() on every IRQ; the low bits of the TSC
+ *                DELTA between consecutive interrupts are accumulated into
+ *                a pool and an estimate of observed variation is counted.
